    "content": "Anne Arundel County Transit Routes Public transit in Anne Arundel County centers on the MTA bus system and MARC train. Routes connect the county to Baltimore and DC, plus local circulation within communities.\nMTA Commuter Bus Routes The Maryland Transit Administration runs commuter buses from Anne Arundel to Baltimore and Washington DC. These are your main options for car-free commuting.\nRoute 4 - Glen Burnie to DC Stops in Anne Arundel:\nGlen Burnie MVA (1001 Crain Highway) Glen Burnie Shopping Center Ritchie Highway locations Other stops along Crain Highway DC Stops:\nUnion Station area L’Enfant Plaza Downtown DC stops Schedule:\nMorning: 5:30 AM - 9:00 AM (peak service) Evening: 4:00 PM - 7:30 PM (peak return) Weekend: Limited or no service Cost:\nSingle ride: $2.00 cash, $1.50 with CharmCard Monthly pass: Around $75-95 for unlimited Website: Check current schedules at mtamaryland.com\nRoute 7 - Annapolis to Baltimore Stops in Anne Arundel:\nAnnapolis MVA (200 Calvert Street) Westgate Center Route 50 corridor Severna Park area Baltimore Stops:\nTimonium area Downtown Baltimore Other route-specific stops Schedule:\nWeekdays: Multiple trips both directions Peak times: Every 30-60 minutes Evenings and weekends: Reduced service Cost:\nSingle ride: $2.00 cash, $1.50 with CharmCard Monthly pass: $75 for unlimited selected routes Route 12 - Severna Park to Baltimore Stops in Anne Arundel:\nSeverna Park MVA (750 Ritchie Highway) Ritchie Highway corridor Severna Park village Baltimore Stops:\nTimonium Downtown routes Specific stops along route Schedule:\nWeekday peak hours primarily Limited evening service Weekend service varies by season Cost: Same as other MTA commuter routes\nRoute 22 - Crofton to DC Stops in Anne Arundel:\nCrofton Center area Defense Highway corridor Southern Anne Arundel locations DC Stops:\nUnion Station Downtown stops L’Enfant Plaza area Schedule:\nMorning rush: 5:45 AM - 9:00 AM Evening rush: 4:15 PM - 8:00 PM Limited midday and weekend service Cost: Standard MTA commuter rates\nRoute 5 - Annapolis to BWI Stops:\nAnnapolis to BWI Airport Connects transit to airport Use Case: Good for catching flights without driving\nRoute Information CharmCard:\nReloadable transit card Discounted fares with card vs cash Available at MTA offices, vending machines Works on all MTA services Mobile Payment:\nSome routes accept mobile payment Check MTA website for current options Real-Time Tracking:\nMTA has app for route tracking Check current arrivals before heading to stop MTA Local Bus Routes MTA also operates local routes within Anne Arundel County. These connect neighborhoods and shopping areas.\nLocal Route Examples Route 100 series: Annapolis local circulation Route 200 series: Glen Burnie area Route 300 series: Severna Park/Odenton Route 400 series: Crofton area\nSchedule:\nGenerally Monday-Saturday service Reduced Sunday service Evenings end by 7-8 PM typically Cost:\n$2.00 cash, $1.50 with CharmCard Free transfers within 2 hours Note: Local routes change frequently. Check current schedules on MTA website.\nMARC Train The MARC Penn Line runs from BWI Rail Station to Baltimore and DC.\nBWI Rail Station Location: BWI Airport Marriott Drive, adjacent to airport\nStops:\nBWI Rail Station (Anne Arundel County) Baltimore Union Station Washington Union Station Schedule Details To Washington DC:\nMorning peak: ~6:00-9:00 AM Evening peak: ~4:00-7:00 PM Travel time: 45-50 minutes No weekend service (Amtrak serves this route) To Baltimore:\nMore frequent throughout day Travel time: 20-25 minutes Some weekend service available Tickets Monthly Passes:\nBWI to DC: Around $150-180 BWI to Baltimore: Around $100-120 Zone pricing applies Single Ride:\nDC: $5.75-12.00 Baltimore: $3.50-6.00 Purchase at station or online Reserve Seats:\nAvailable for additional fee Guarantees seat on busy trains Book ahead online MARC Website Current schedules and info: marylandtransit.com/marc\nLocal Shuttle Services Anne Arundel County Shuttle AACTransit:\nSome county-funded shuttle services Connects government buildings Sometimes serves senior centers Contact: 410-222-7000 for current routes\nSenior Transit AAA Transit (Area Agency on Aging):\nTransportation for seniors 60+ Medical appointments Shopping trips Application required Contact: Area Agency on Aging office\nSpecial Event Shuttles Annapolis Events:\nSmartFuel Sailing Week shuttle Fall Festival overflow parking shuttle Blues Festival transport Check County Website: Current event shuttle info posted before major events\nFerry Services St. Leonard Ferry Route: St. Leonard to Solomons Island\nCost: Free\nSchedule:\nRuns 24/7 Frequency varies by time of day Wait times 5-30 minutes typically Use Case: Connects southern Anne Arundel to Calvert County and Eastern Shore via ferry\nWebsite: Maryland Transportation Authority ferry info\nParatransit Services MTA Access Link Eligibility:\nMust have disability preventing use of regular bus Application and certification required Door-to-door or curb-to-curb service Service Area:\nWithin 3/4 mile of MTA bus routes County-wide coverage Reservation:\nCall ahead required Same-day service sometimes available Advance booking recommended Cost: Same as regular bus fare\nContact: MTA Access Link office for application\nPlanning Your Trip MTA Trip Planner Website: mtamaryland.com has trip planning tool\nWhat it provides:\nRoute options Schedule times Transfer information Real-time updates Recommended Apps MTA Transit App:\nOfficial MTA app Route info and schedules Service alerts Google Maps:\nTransit directions Real-time bus locations Good for trip planning Tips for Transit Users Peak vs Off-Peak:\nCommuter buses fill up during rush hour Arrive 10-15 minutes early Consider flexible schedules if possible CharmCard Benefits:\nCheaper than cash fares Easy to reload Works across all MTA services Weekend Service:\nLimited compared to weekdays Plan ahead for trips Some routes don’t run Sundays Cold Weather:\nBus stops may not be heated Have warm clothes ready Check for weather delays Luggage:\nCommuter buses have space for bags Check baggage policies for specific routes Service Changes \u0026 Alerts Schedule Changes:\nRoutes adjust seasonally Holiday schedules posted in advance Summer vs winter schedules differ Service Alerts:\nMTA website posts delays Text alerts available for subscribers Check before trips during weather events Contact Information MTA Customer Service: 1-888-968-7282\nMARC Train Info: 1-877-687-6272\nCharmCard Support: 410-768-3600\nMTA Website: www.mtamaryland.com\nFor more transportation info:\nCommuting Guide Parking Guide BWI Airport Guide Official Government Resources Anne Arundel County Government Official County Website\nMain County Site: www.aacounty.org County Services: www.aacounty.org/departments OpenData Portal: data.aacounty.org Maryland State Government Official State Portal\nMD.gov: maryland.gov State Departments: maryland.gov/agencies State Services: maryland.gov/services Last updated: May 2026\nLast updated: May 2026",
