    "breadcrumb": "",
    "content": "Welcome to Anne Arundel County Anne Arundel County is a vibrant region on the Chesapeake Bay with over 1.5 million residents, diverse communities, and a mix of urban, suburban, and rural living. From the historic capital of Annapolis to the family-friendly neighborhoods of Severna Park and Crofton, our county offers something for everyone.\nExplore Cities \u0026 Communities Discover detailed guides for every community in Anne Arundel County:\nArnold - Charming waterfront town on the Severn River with a historic downtown and ferry to Annapolis Crofton - Family-friendly community with excellent schools and proximity to Fort Meade Crownsville - Historic eastern community with Chesapeake Bay beaches Davidsonville - Waterfront town on the Patuxent River with boat ramps and parks Deale - Small waterfront community with quiet coastal living Fort Meade - Major military installation home to NSA and CIA Gambrills - Suburban community near Historic London Town Glen Burnie - Largest community with diverse neighborhoods and shopping Millersville - Suburban community near Fort Meade with family-friendly neighborhoods Odenton - Growing community with new downtown and excellent schools Parole - Rural community with countryside living and horse farms Pasadena - Waterfront community with Chesapeake Bay views and marinas Severna Park - Top-rated schools and walkable downtown Severn - Suburban community along the Severn River near Annapolis Sunnydale - Quiet residential community in eastern Anne Arundel County Things to Do Anne Arundel County offers 15+ major attractions including state parks, trails, historic sites, and museums:\nSandy Point State Park - 6,500 acres on the Chesapeake Bay with beaches, camping, and kayaking BWI Trail - 5.7-mile paved recreational trail from Glen Burnie to Arundel Mills Baltimore \u0026 Annapolis Trail - 14-mile rail trail connecting Annapolis to Baltimore Maryland State House - Oldest capitol building in continuous legislative use Quiet Waters Park - Zoo, nature center, playground, and tennis courts in Annapolis Historic London Town \u0026 Gardens - Restored 18th-century colonial buildings and gardens North Point State Park - Historic site where the Star-Spangled Banner was inspired Patuxent River State Park - 6,700 acres with camping, hiking, and water sports View all attractions →\nPractical Guides In-depth resources for living in Anne Arundel County:\nMoving \u0026 Settling In Settling In Guide - Your first 30 days checklist Transportation \u0026 Commuting - I-95, MARC, MTA, ferries, and parking BWI Airport Guide - Complete airport access and parking guide Housing \u0026 Budgeting Housing Guide - Home values, rental market, and neighborhoods Housing Cost Calculator - Estimate your housing budget by town Cost of Living - Detailed budgeting breakdown Tax Guide - Property, income, and sales taxes Utility Costs - Electric, water, gas, and internet costs Schools \u0026 Education Schools \u0026 Education - Complete AACPS guide with ratings School Enrollment Guide - Step-by-step enrollment process Military Education - DoDEA, GI Bill, and military benefits Healthcare Healthcare Guide - Hospitals, doctors, and insurance Pediatric Care - Finding pediatricians for your children Tricare Guide - Health insurance for military families Veterans \u0026 Military Veterans \u0026 Military Resources - Fort Meade resources, VA benefits, and family services Military Employment - Job search and career transition About This Guide AnneArundelGuide.com provides comprehensive, fact-checked information about Anne Arundel County, Maryland. Our content is based on official government sources, local data, and verified information to help you make informed decisions about living, working, and visiting this wonderful region.\nLast updated: May 2026",
    "description": "The authoritative guide to Anne Arundel County, MD - comprehensive resources for Annapolis, Glen Burnie, Severna Park, Crofton \u0026 more. Cost of living, schools, healthcare, transportation, and local living tips.",
